    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "762c9430_d1792710",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 924,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124693
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-06T06:43:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In what situation would this be NULL? I would expect that channel is present if we are handling an event. (Same question for other trace_trusty_ipc_*)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 924,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 924,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "3b6b7debc9c834ea4936035c76c49b13ae9fe580",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "611d9464_6777c602",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 924,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-18T23:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might never be NULL. I added the check to make sure we don\u0027t crash because of the added trace point if any these functions can be called when `dn-\u003echan` is NULL. If we go though the code and make sure that can\u0027t happen, then this guard can be removed. This function already has a code path where it assumes `dn-\u003echan` is a valid pointer, so I think there is a good chance that this function will never be called with a NULL `dn-\u003echan`.  The other functions with similar trace points don\u0027t touch `dn-\u003echan` though.",
      "parentUuid": "762c9430_d1792710",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 924,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 924,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "3b6b7debc9c834ea4936035c76c49b13ae9fe580",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b4fbb20_2d64c984",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-ipc.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 924,
      "author": {
        "id": 1902326
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-14T19:40:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As best I can tell, we never seem to null check the `tipc_msg_buf*` pointers that get passed into functions. So I suspect it\u0027s safe to access `dn-\u003echan-\u003elocal` without an additional null check, since the assumption is that a null value should never be passed in.",
      "parentUuid": "611d9464_6777c602",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 924,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 924,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "3b6b7debc9c834ea4936035c76c49b13ae9fe580",
